1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,514
You hear your voice on a recording and think: “Is that really me?”

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:08,642
When you speak, your voice reaches your ears by two paths at once.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:14,675
1 — Through the air: sound leaves your mouth and travels into your ears.

4
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:20,538
2 — Through your bones: vibrations travel through your skull to your inner ear.

5
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:26,230
Bone conduction carries low tones well, so your voice sounds deeper and fuller to you.

6
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:31,761
A recording only captures the air version — the voice everyone else hears.

7
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,936
So the recording is closer to your real voice.

8
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:37,687
With time, you get used to it.
